    "explanation": {
      "latex": "Let $S_n = \\sum_{k=1}^n a_k = 6n^3$.\nThe $n$-th term is $a_n = S_n - S_{n-1} = 6n^3 - 6(n-1)^3 = 6(n^3 - (n^3 - 3n^2 + 3n - 1)) = 18n^2 - 18n + 6$.\nWe need to evaluate $a_{k+1} - a_k$:\n$a_{k+1} = 18(k+1)^2 - 18(k+1) + 6 = 18(k^2 + 2k + 1) - 18k - 18 + 6 = 18k^2 + 18k + 6$.\n$a_{k+1} - a_k = (18k^2 + 18k + 6) - (18k^2 - 18k + 6) = 36k$.\nSubstitute this back into the desired sum:\n$\\sum_{k=1}^6 \\left( \\frac{36k}{36} \\right)^2 = \\sum_{k=1}^6 k^2 = 1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + 4^2 + 5^2 + 6^2 = \\frac{6(6+1)(2 \\cdot 6 + 1)}{6} = \\frac{6 \\times 7 \\times 13}{6} = 91$.",
      "unicode": "Let S_n = sum_{k=1}^n a_k = 6n³.\nThe n-th term is a_n = S_n - S_{n-1} = 6n³ - 6(n-1)³ = 6(n³ - (n³ - 3n² + 3n - 1)) = 18n² - 18n + 6.\nWe need to evaluate a_{k+1} - a_k:\na_{k+1} = 18(k+1)² - 18(k+1) + 6 = 18(k² + 2k + 1) - 18k - 18 + 6 = 18k² + 18k + 6.\na_{k+1} - a_k = (18k² + 18k + 6) - (18k² - 18k + 6) = 36k.\nSubstitute this back into the desired sum:\nsum_{k=1}^6 left( (36k/36) right)² = sum_{k=1}^6 k² = 1² + 2² + 3² + 4² + 5² + 6² = (6(6+1)(2 · 6 + 1)/6) = (6 × 7 × 13/6) = 91.",
      "plainText": "Let S_n = sum_{k=1}^n a_k = 6n^3. The n-th term is a_n = S_n - S_{n-1} = 6n^3 - 6(n-1)^3 = 6(n^3 - (n^3 - 3n^2 + 3n - 1)) = 18n^2 - 18n + 6. We need to evaluate a_{k+1} - a_k: a_{k+1} = 18(k+1)^2 - 18(k+1) + 6 = 18(k^2 + 2k + 1) - 18k - 18 + 6 = 18k^2 + 18k + 6. a_{k+1} - a_k = (18k^2 + 18k + 6) - (18k^2 - 18k + 6) = 36k. Substitute this back into the desired sum: sum_{k=1}^6 left( (36k)/(36) right)^2 = sum_{k=1}^6 k^2 = 1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + 4^2 + 5^2 + 6^2 = (6(6+1)(2 cdot 6 + 1))/(6) = (6 times 7 times 13)/(6) = 91."
